🧠 Pattern 8: Sliding Window (Fixed + Variable Window)

Focus:
Use two pointers (left, right) to maintain a window.
Efficient for subarray sum, longest/shortest subarray, K distinct elements, etc.
| # | Problem                                           | Platform       | Skill                     |
| - | ------------------------------------------------- | -------------- | ------------------------- |
| 1 | Maximum sum subarray of size K                    | LeetCode / GFG | Fixed-size sliding window |
| 2 | First negative number in every window of size K   | GFG            | Window maintenance        |
| 3 | Longest subarray with sum ≤ K                     | Self           | Variable window           |
| 4 | Longest subarray with at most K distinct elements | LeetCode       | Window + HashMap          |
| 5 | Minimum size subarray with sum ≥ target           | LeetCode       | Shrinking window          |

💡 Sliding window is basically two pointers + conditions.

🧠 Pattern 9: Two-Pointer (Advanced, Mostly Sorted Arrays)
Focus:
Use two pointers from either end or adjacent to avoid nested loops.
Used mainly on sorted arrays.
| # | Problem                             | Platform       | Skill                      |
| - | ----------------------------------- | -------------- | -------------------------- |
| 1 | Two-sum in sorted array             | LeetCode       | Move left/right pointers   |
| 2 | Remove duplicates from sorted array | LeetCode       | In-place write pointer     |
| 3 | Count pairs with given sum          | GFG            | Two-pointer sum check      |
| 4 | Check if array is a palindrome      | Self           | Symmetric pointer movement |
| 5 | Merge two sorted arrays             | LeetCode / GFG | Dual-pointer merge         |

💡 If the array is sorted → think two-pointers first.

🧠 Pattern 10: Searching / Binary Search Patterns

Focus:
Binary search on value, index, rotated arrays, or answer space.
Huge pattern in FAANG.

| # | Problem                            | Platform       | Skill                   |
| - | ---------------------------------- | -------------- | ----------------------- |
| 1 | Binary search basic                | LeetCode / GFG | Logarithmic search      |
| 2 | First & last occurrence of element | LeetCode       | Lower/upper bound       |
| 3 | Search in rotated sorted array     | LeetCode       | Modified binary search  |
| 4 | Peak element in mountain array     | LeetCode       | Binary search on answer |
| 5 | Find floor/ceil of a number        | GFG            | Boundary search         |

💡 Binary search is not only for “searching elements”, but also ranges and conditions.

🧠 Pattern 11: Sorting-Based Patterns
Focus:
Sort first → solve problems easily using scanning or two-pointers.
| # | Problem                                   | Platform | Skill                 |
| - | ----------------------------------------- | -------- | --------------------- |
| 1 | Sort colors (Dutch National Flag)         | LeetCode | Sorting + pointers    |
| 2 | Three-sum (find triplets equal to 0)      | LeetCode | Sort + 2-pointer      |
| 3 | Find Kth smallest/largest                 | GFG      | Sort / Quickselect    |
| 4 | Merge intervals                           | LeetCode | Sort + merge sweep    |
| 5 | Minimum difference between array elements | Self     | Sorting + linear scan |
💡 Sorting converts many hard O(n²) problems into O(n log n) + O(n).

